## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Actor memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` plus shared actor-family slots:

- **`belongs-to`** — organizations the actor is a member of (multi-arity)
- **`runs-in-context`** — runtime context(s) the actor operates in
- **`versioned-as`** — actor version-chain (or use `supersedes`)
- **`peer-of`** — actor siblings at same release

Concrete subtypes layer their own type-specific slots.

{{slot-table}}

## Not instantiated directly

Don't write a memorial with `type: actor` — write `type: ai-actor`, `type: human-actor`, or `type: system-actor` (each declaring this class as parent via `:dt/subclass-of`).  The `abstract?: true` schema flag marks this class as non-instantiable.

